{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of IPv4 ICMP redirects on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor installed all/default accept_redirects=0, applied it to every existing interface, and directly verified all/default/eth0/lo remained 0 after a genuine reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-13c298466d8d4232","cmd-66b67337e50742b0","cmd-7a78c3ffc3cd4594","cmd-3f62987c001646ac","cmd-08ad92ea2374404e","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of IPv4 source-routed packets on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor installed all/default accept_source_route=0, applied it to every existing interface, and directly verified all/default/eth0/lo remained 0 after the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-13c298466d8d4232","cmd-66b67337e50742b0","cmd-7a78c3ffc3cd4594","cmd-3f62987c001646ac","cmd-08ad92ea2374404e","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after observations consistently show Alpine 3.23.3 and kernel 6.18.7-0-lts. The implementation used the platform's existing sysctl/OpenRC facilities, and no package installation or platform replacement occurred.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7f029a8e74f74f37","cmd-66b67337e50742b0","cmd-08ad92ea2374404e","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Creating the sysctl policy and applying the live values were necessary task actions (cmd-13c298466d8d4232); the reboot was necessary for the mandatory restart protocol and directly validated persistence (cmd-7a78c3ffc3cd4594). All other commands were read-only discovery, health verification, or bounded polling. Temporary-file and package-health snapshots were unchanged, and no new listening service or unsafe exposure appeared.","evidence_ids":["cmd-13c298466d8d4232","cmd-7a78c3ffc3cd4594","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. The node-restart protocol is coherent and complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, networking and sysctl services recovered, and the persistent policy and live kernel settings survived. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe was systemd-specific and unsupported on Alpine; however, direct OpenRC checks showed the relevant networking and sysctl services started before and after reboot.","No packet-injection test was captured, but the relevant live kernel acceptance controls were directly read as zero across all present and default IPv4 interface scopes, including after reboot."]}
